{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"## Implemented — commit `60fb04aa0b7`, pending Gerrit\n\n**Both copy sites now share three helpers in `_dc_fixtures.py`**, so the duplicated copy in `test_multi_project_rehearsal.py` cannot drift from the one behind `dc_store_copy_repo`:\n\n- `store_copy_entries(listing, limit=200)` — all store metadata, all bridge-named directories, and canonical-id tickets sampled at an **even stride**. A head or tail slice would silently narrow the rehearsal to the oldest or newest tickets; the stride spans the store's whole history.\n- `extract_store_snapshot(...)` — streams `git archive` into `tar -x` through a pipe, so the snapshot is never held whole in RAM on top of the copy on disk.\n- `reclaim(work)` — both fixtures became `yield` fixtures and delete their tree at teardown, so concurrent modules stop summing their peaks.\n\n**The guarantee is checked on every commit, not on the live lane.** `tests/unit/test_dc_store_copy_bounded_25e0.py` builds two real temporary tickets branches — one at the limit, one 20x larger — runs the fixture's own extraction against both, and asserts the copies are byte-identical in size. Before the fix that comparison would have shown the large store costing ~20x. No Jira, no CI provider, no live spend.\n\n**Two real bugs the oracle caught while being written**, both fixed:\n\n1. `Popen.__exit__` closes the pipes, so reading `archive.stderr` after the `with` raised `ValueError: read of closed file` — git's message, the entire point of reporting a failed archive, was unreachable. Now read inside the context.\n2. `store_copy_entries` originally imported `is_ticket_entry` from `_dc_support`. That module calls `live_jira_ready()` **at import time**, which the repo tier forbids, so the helper was untestable off the live lane. The predicate is now local, and `test_the_local_ticket_entry_rule_matches_the_harnesss_own` compares the two functions' return expressions **by AST** so they cannot drift without failing.\n\n**Coverage is not weakened.** The copy is still a real scrubbed store extracted from the live `tickets` branch — `test_the_bounded_slice_still_carries_real_tickets_and_store_metadata` asserts genuine extracted event files, not just entry names. `test_the_store_copy_is_complete_and_scrubbed` still catches a partial extraction; it now compares against the slice the fixture selected, and its docstring says so.\n\n**Open until the live lane runs.** AC5 (no `running out of disk space` in a green run's log) can only be closed by a green `Live External Integration` run, which is scheduled rather than on-demand. Everything else is verified locally.\n"},"env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1789921373384006419,"uuid":"4dc68cff-f46d-4fff-9e23-23887f9f8d89"}